# MikroTik vendor attributes.
#
# Only what this server sends on an Access-Accept. The `radius` package ships the
# RFC dictionaries but no vendor ones, and Mikrotik-Rate-Limit is how a MikroTik
# applies a PPP rate limit without the RouterOS API — it is the whole reason an ISP
# runs RADIUS instead of provisioning every secret by hand.
#
# Syntax is the FreeRADIUS one the package's parser reads. Note the vendor id is
# repeated on every VENDORATTR line: the parser takes
# `VENDORATTR <vendor-id> <name> <attribute-id> <type>` and does not inherit the
# enclosing BEGIN-VENDOR block for it.

VENDOR MikroTik 14988

BEGIN-VENDOR MikroTik

VENDORATTR 14988 Mikrotik-Rate-Limit 8 string
VENDORATTR 14988 Mikrotik-Recv-Limit 9 integer
VENDORATTR 14988 Mikrotik-Host-IP 16 ipaddr
VENDORATTR 14988 Mikrotik-Group 24 string

END-VENDOR MikroTik
